### Scenario 32 — Admin deactivates a user (emits USER_DEACTIVATED via Outbox+Kafka)
### IntelliJ HTTP Client syntax.
### Prereq: admin seeded via SQL (see sql/init_auth_service.sql).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@adminEmail = admin@blps.local
@adminPass = adminpass

### 32.1 Register a throwaway tenant (idempotent — 409 means it already exists)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "deactivateme@blps.local", "password": "tmppass1", "role": "TENANT" }

> {%
if (response.status === 201 && response.body && response.body.id) {
  client.global.set("deact32_id", response.body.id);
}
%}

### 32.2 If 409 above, look the user up (admin)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

> {%
if (Array.isArray(response.body)) {
  const u = response.body.find(x => x.email === "deactivateme@blps.local");
  if (u) client.global.set("deact32_id", u.id);
}
%}

### 32.3 Read user (admin)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{deact32_id}}
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

### 32.4 Deactivate user (privilege USER_DEACTIVATE)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{deact32_id}}/deactivate
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

### 32.5 Confirm enabled=false
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{deact32_id}}
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

### 32.6 Disabled user can no longer authenticate (expect 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Basic deactivateme@blps.local tmppass1

### 32.7 Idempotency — second deactivate is a no-op (no new event)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{deact32_id}}/deactivate
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
